      "from": "The server/client code is an original Node.js/DOM implementation using standard-library cryptographic primitives. It imports no upstream implementation or prior lab reconstruction.",
      "to": "The server/client use native Node.js/DOM code and standard-library cryptographic primitives. The bounded history slice is source-assisted and retains GPL-2.0-or-later attribution to KeePass2.61.1; production execution imports no upstream runtime or prior lab reconstruction."
    },
    {
      "from": "## Entry history and safe editor publication\n\nChanged entry content creates an encrypted previous version. Imported count/size limits prune supported flat history using released source ordering; a no-op save updates access without creating a version. History previews are explicit and masked by default. Confirmed restoration preserves current identity/location and backs up the current entry. Unsaved editor values refuse Restore before an effect; drafts entered during pending Save/Restore are retained. View cleanup cancels its owned timer and prevents disposed responses from republishing private fields.\n\nThis finite source-assisted slice is documented in the [preserved study README](results/history-followup/stage/README.md.snapshot), [source contracts](results/history-followup/stage/SOURCE-CONTRACTS.md.snapshot), [draft/lifecycle correction](results/history-followup/stage/DRAFT-CORRECTION.md.snapshot) and [license notice](results/history-followup/NOTICE.md). Exact sources, original failures and historical receipts remain inert snapshots under results/history-followup/stage/. The original181/selection546/current1454 evidence and compatibility18 retain their own source identities. The application uses native JavaScript; original assembly execution occurs only in test tooling. Finite helper/DOM/HTTP evidence does not establish complete KeePass parity, original GUI execution or security/performance superiority. The full original ZIP and release executable remain local study/oracle carriers.\n",
      "to": "## Entry history and safe editor publication\n\nChanged content creates an encrypted previous version; a no-op save updates access without a new revision. Explicit history previews start masked. Confirmed restoration backs up the current entry, restores represented fields/metadata and preserves its identity, placement and maintained history. Restore refuses unsaved editor changes before an effect. Drafts entered during pending Save/Restore and newer selections survive late responses. View cleanup cancels its timer and blocks disposed publications. Imported count/size limits apply within the documented local bounds.\n\n[HISTORY.md](HISTORY.md) describes the exact supported fields, pruning/deviation bounds, fixture prerequisites, source/licensing citations and remaining manual/product gaps. The source-bound current-layout adapter passed 41 focused groups and separately replayed 11 author-run probes. The accepted independent review separately passed 11 probes and actual private-browser held-response/restore/restart checks. The focused original campaign made 24 authenticated assembly loads; its edit ordering was partly source-composed, with original GUI and original Touch execution counts 0. These campaigns remain separate. Historical compatibility18 retains its original sources.\n\nThe [current preservation manifest](results/history-followup/preservation-manifest.json) maps the original 1454 stage to 1442 public inert snapshots and 12 local-only source ZIP payloads (four named and eight acquisition copies). The bundle contains 1656 total public evidence files, including the final 82-artifact independent review and historical failures. Public .local directory segments are mapped to private-study-records; original paths/hashes remain recorded. No original EXE/DLL/source ZIP bytes are embedded publicly. See the [source-assisted license notice](results/history-followup/NOTICE.md) and exact released licenses linked there. Full parity, original-grade security and superiority remain unestablished.\n"
    }
  ],
  "newHistoryFile": "HISTORY.md",
  "runtimeChanges": 0,
  "oldEvidenceChanged": false,
